/-!
# Algebraization of a completion quotient with torsion conormal

Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Tag 0ALR, lemma-quotient-by-idempotent
(blueprint: lem-per-conormal-torsion-algebraization).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v w

namespace AdicCompletion

/-- A quotient of a completed finite type algebra whose conormal is killed by a power of
the ideal of definition is the completion of a finite type algebra.

Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Tag 0ALR, lemma-quotient-by-idempotent
(blueprint: lem-per-conormal-torsion-algebraization).

Proof. Put S = B completed along IB. Finite type permanence and Noetherian completion
make B and S Noetherian, with S complete and S/IS = B/IB. The kernel J is finitely
generated. The hypothesis implies f^c J is contained in J^2 for f in IS, so J_f is an
idempotent ideal; a finitely generated idempotent ideal is generated by an idempotent.
Thus C_f is an idempotent localization of S_f, including when c = 0.
The punctured idempotent complement lemma supplies a quotient C' with S_f isomorphic
to (C × C')_f for every f in IS. The product T = C × C' is finite over S.
Choose generators f_i of IB. Glue the completed algebra T to the charts B localized
at f_i, using the inverses of these isomorphisms. The double-localization maps agree,
and the chart swaps satisfy the cocycle identity because they reorder denominators.
Flatness of B → S and the isomorphism modulo IB let finite-algebra formal glueing
produce a finite B-algebra D with D tensor S isomorphic to T.
The idempotent (1,0) modulo IT corresponds to an idempotent modulo ID. Since D is
integral over B, lift it to an idempotent e after an etale replacement B → B' which
is an isomorphism modulo IB. The algebra B' is flat and finite type over B, hence
Noetherian and finite type over A; D' = D tensor B' is finite over B'.
Flatness and the isomorphism modulo I imply isomorphisms modulo every power of I.
Their compatible inverses identify the completions of B and B'. Completion of the
finite module D' is tensor product with the completion of B'; tensor associativity
therefore identifies the completion of D' with T, compatibly modulo I.
The finite S-module T is complete, hence (T,IT) is henselian. Uniqueness of lifting
idempotents shows that e maps to (1,0) in T. Split D' as D'/(1-e) × D'/(e).
Both factors are finite type over A. Completion preserves this product, and the
factor selected by e therefore has completion A-algebra isomorphic to C. -/
theorem exists_finiteType_algebraization_of_conormal_torsion
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (I : Ideal A)
    (B : Type v) [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
    (hB : RingHom.FiniteType (algebraMap A B))
    (C : Type w) [CommRing C] [Algebra A C]
    (f : AdicCompletion (I.map (algebraMap A B)) B →ₐ[A] C)
    (hf : Function.Surjective f)
    (htorsion : ∃ c : ℕ,
      ∀ r ∈ (I ^ c).map
        (algebraMap A (AdicCompletion (I.map (algebraMap A B)) B)),
      ∀ x : (RingHom.ker f.toRingHom).Cotangent, r • x = 0) :
    ∃ (D : Type (max u v)) (_ : CommRing D) (_ : Algebra A D),
      RingHom.FiniteType (algebraMap A D) ∧
      Nonempty (AdicCompletion (I.map (algebraMap A D)) D ≃ₐ[A] C) := by
  sorry

end AdicCompletion
